WEBVTT

00:04:56.542 --> 00:05:00.125
that no other country
has come close to matching.

00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:02.351
And then there's Europe,

00:05:02.375 --> 00:05:04.851
and in Europe a conversation
about the internet

00:05:04.875 --> 00:05:09.226
is effectively a conversation
about data and privacy.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.059
So there you have it:

00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:12.434
one common problem,

00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:16.434
and three increasingly different,
competing views.

00:05:16.458 --> 00:05:19.518
This shows us that rival ideologies

00:05:19.542 --> 00:05:22.726
will drive very distinct
ways of doing things.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:26.768
But what about collaboration
and cooperation?

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:31.059
Well, I'm going to start with the example
of three small countries: